{
 "_": [
  "What catalog_normalize() actually answers, captured from the database.",
  "",
  "GENERATED, NOT WRITTEN. Every \"out\" below came out of a running Postgres by",
  "calling catalog_normalize(<in>, null). It is committed so that CI can check",
  "the TypeScript copy of the fold against the authoritative one without needing",
  "Docker, and so that a change to either is a visible diff rather than a silent",
  "divergence.",
  "",
  "The cases are chosen to hit the places the two implementations can disagree:",
  "letters unaccent EXPANDS rather than strips (ss, ae, oe, th), typography that",
  "reaches product names off packaging (curly quotes, en-dashes, guillemets),",
  "the diacritics of all six languages, and whitespace at both ends and in the",
  "middle. Plain ASCII names are in here too, as the control.",
  "",
  "To regenerate after changing catalog_normalize():",
  "  npx supabase --workdir catalog db reset",
  "  then re-run the generator described in test/catalog/discovery.test.js"
 ],
